## SH1 — Two hops with start, middle and end conditions: how placing the middle condition changes the boundaries
traits: start=filtered scan hops=2 fan-out=low aggregate Top-20 | R1 start: q.view_count | R2 end: u.reputation | R3 middle: a.score | R6 aggregate / sort: u.display_name

### SH1 @graph
StoreQuery[neo4j] out=(u.display_name, answers)
  : Limit[20]
  :   Sort[answers DESC, u.display_name ASC]
  :     Aggregation[keys: u.display_name | count(*) AS answers]
  :       GetProperty(u.display_name) [node:User]
  :         Filter((u.reputation >= 1000))
  :           GetProperty(u.reputation) [node:User]
  :             Expand((a)<-[_r1:AUTHORED]-(u:User))
  :               Filter((a.score >= 10))
  :                 GetProperty(a.score) [node:Post]
  :                   Expand((q)-[_r0:PARENT_OF]->(a:Post))
  :                     Filter((q.view_count >= 10000))
  :                       GetProperty(q.view_count) [node:Post]
  :                         EntityScan(q:Post)

### SH1 @relational
Coord Limit[20]
  Coord Sort[answers DESC, u.display_name ASC]
    Coord Aggregation[keys: u.display_name | count(*) AS answers]
      StoreQuery[mysql] in=(u) out=(u, u.display_name)
        : GetProperty(u.display_name) [node:User]
        :   Filter((u.reputation >= 1000))
        :     GetProperty(u.reputation) [node:User]
        :       Argument(u)
        StoreQuery[mysql] in=(a) out=(a)
          : Filter((a.score >= 10))
          :   GetProperty(a.score) [node:Post]
          :     Argument(a)
          StoreQuery[neo4j] in=(q) out=(q, a, u)
            : Expand((a)<-[_r1:AUTHORED]-(u:User))
            :   Expand((q)-[_r0:PARENT_OF]->(a:Post))
            :     Argument(q)
            StoreQuery[mysql] out=(q)
              : Filter((q.view_count >= 10000))
              :   GetProperty(q.view_count) [node:Post]
              :     EntityScan(q:Post)

